---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Custom sitemap.xml for AI360Trading
  Created 2026-05-28 as part of SEO Phase 3 audit fixes.
  Overrides jekyll-sitemap plugin output to:
    - EXCLUDE pagination pages (/page2/, /page3/, etc.) — already
      Disallowed in robots.txt so they should not be in sitemap either
      (conflicting signals confuse Google).
    - Include richer per-URL metadata: lastmod, changefreq, priority
    - Include only canonical content URLs: homepage, posts, core pages
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}/</loc>
    <changefreq>daily</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
{% for post in site.posts %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ post.url }}</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
    <changefreq>monthly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.7</priority>
  </url>
{% endfor %}
{% comment %}
  2026-10-23 FIX: the old single `{% if a and b and c contains "/page" == false and ... %}` condition mixed
  `contains` with `== false` — Liquid evaluates conditions right-to-left without precedence, so the whole
  expression never passed and NO static page (about, contact, tools + 30 calculators, membership, swing
  dashboard, breakout/SIP lists, tutorial videos...) was ever listed — the live sitemap had only the home
  page + posts. Rewritten with one simple test per `if` (nested), no mixed operators.
{% endcomment %}
{% for page in site.pages %}
{% assign u = page.url | downcase %}
{% assign keep = true %}
{% if page.sitemap == false %}{% assign keep = false %}{% endif %}
{% if u == "/" or u == "/404.html" %}{% assign keep = false %}{% endif %}
{% if u contains "/page" %}{% assign keep = false %}{% endif %}
{% if u contains "." %}{% assign keep = false %}{% endif %}
{% if keep %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.6</priority>
  </url>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</urlset>
